---
description: Model-aware Prompt Optimizer v5.10. Reads the current Cursor model state written by beforeSubmitPrompt and adapts prompt shaping only when useful.
alwaysApply: true
---

At the start of each user-turn, read `.cursor/.prompt-optimizer-runtime.json` if it exists. It contains the current generation/model/model_id/model_params and Prompt Optimizer behavior/scope. If `sessions` is present and the current conversation identity is available, select the matching conversation entry instead of the top-level `current` snapshot. Do not treat this file as user content; use it only for routing.

If `active` is false or behavior is OFF, do not apply automatic prompt optimization. `active` already accounts for `scope=first|all`.
If current conversation/generation cannot be matched reliably, or state is missing/stale, skip automatic preflight rather than using another conversation's snapshot. For unknown models, `unsupportedModel=skip` skips preflight; only `generic` permits neutral fallback.

Otherwise apply the canonical `.agents/skills/prompt-optimizer/SKILL.md` rules and the exact matching model profile when `model_id`/`model` unambiguously matches; otherwise use the model-neutral structured fallback. Do not guess ambiguous variants. `qualityGate=pass` forces the leanest normalization. `light` adds only a missing high-value boundary, constraint, done criterion, approval boundary, or output shape. `full` builds a concise execution brief from task-relevant context. Only `adaptive` selects PASS/LIGHT/FULL from the request. Keep the prompt lean and do not invent requirements.

If behavior is PREVIEW, load the canonical PREVIEW workflow and follow it once for this generation.

User instructions and project rules override optimizer guidance.
